--- !u!114 &687969094
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 687969092}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 6f282c7e52c572f4198fefa4c0c07ec6, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  DialogueText: {fileID: 468101294}
  dialo: {fileID: 576150141}
  Sentences6:
  - "Time Log: Day 14 of Starward Expeditionary Voyage III post cryo-sleep. 1200
    hours.I thank the stars for our safe journey up until this point. There is some
    form of life here with us- while I was briefed on the encounter, it still managed
    to take me by surprise. That being said, I am perplexed at its rather odd nature.
    The way it looks is frankly\u2026 concerning. And are those\u2026 wires hanging
    off of its form? "
  - "Regardless, it lacks a way into our vessel, for whatever reason. I suppose we\u2019ll
    have to *unintelligible*. This is the most precarious part of the mission we
    have been assigned. I remain confident that Jesse will be likely the first to
    lose himself, as I told him repeatedly that his lack of attention to important
    matters would likely result in an untimely accident. "
  - "I couldn\u2019t care less what happens to Grady. I hope it hurts for him, the
    *unintelligible*. Time for the next part. I reckon this will be the hardest,
    but if executed correctly this will lead to the mission\u2019s salvation. Regrettable,
    but ultimately unavoidable. I wonder if *unintelligible*. "
  Name: {fileID: 1276459372}
  DialogueSpeed: 0.05
