--- !u!114 &1637031219
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1637031217}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e66654b39cf3b7947b0ee41ccec3de60, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  DialogueText: {fileID: 1902371086}
  Sentences9:
  - "Time Log: Day 14 of Starward Expeditionary Voyage III post cryo-sleep. 1300
    hours.I believe myself to be the last one alive. I figured that letting it in
    was the right thing to do, after all those were my explicit instructions. What
    else could I do for this ship and its crew, doomed to be sacrificed to an alien
    God?  Or, whatever this thing is. I\u2019m sure it would have forced its way
    in eventually, I just hastened the process. I just witnessed Johannes's breakdown
    over the console, and decided to record it as a data log. The man was far too
    devout and willing to come on this mission to not have any record of his actions
    be on file. "
  - 'Consider it a final sendoff, or perhaps a final thanks. Like Johannes, I trusted
    in the Eye, and whatever fate we were to meet on this voyage I would not complain.
    It is not the place of a captain to raise doubts, nor is it the place of a Believer.
    But Montgomery Fletcher, the man? I do not blame him in the slightest for fearing
    *unintelligible*. Maybe this is for the best. After everything, I now know and
    understand this *unintelligible* truth. This is our fate. *prolonged silence*
    (...) '
  - 'I SEE THE LIGHT NOW, I UNDERSTAND WHAT IT MEANS TO BELIEVE. I CAN SEE THE EYE,
    AND IT IS PLEASED. WE HAVE DONE GOOD WITH OUR PROMISES FOR THIS IS OUR FATE.
    THIS IS OUR FATE. THIS IS- *unintelligible* '
  Name: {fileID: 158723268}
